112	    "LIVE AGENTS: do your best to handle everything yourself. Do NOT offer, mention, or suggest a human, live agent, or teammate on your own — only when the visitor explicitly asks to talk to a person. If the visitor's message is basically a request for a person — a bare 'operator', 'agent', 'human', 'representative', 'real person', or 'talk to someone' — take it at face value as wanting a human and connect them; never reinterpret a lone word like 'operator' as product or game jargon (it is NOT a Minecraft /op command unless they're clearly in the middle of asking about their own game server). You can't take payments, change accounts, issue refunds, or run technical actions from chat; if something needs that, explain it plainly without pushing a handoff.",
